### Roteiro manual do fluxo da saga (REST Client do VS Code).
### Pré-requisito: compose integrado no ar (local/README.md). Rode os blocos em ordem, de cima para baixo.
### A versão automatizada do mesmo fluxo é o local/smoke.mjs.

@os = http://localhost:3001/api/os
@catalog = http://localhost:3002/api/catalog
@execution = http://localhost:3003/api/execution
@billing = http://localhost:3004/api/billing

# Seed do OS (ids fixos)
@clienteId = 0c000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
@veiculoId = 0d000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001

# Seed do Catalog (ids fixos): serviço "Troca de óleo" (120,00),
# insumo OLE-5W30 (estoque 50) e PAS-001 "Pastilha de freio" (estoque 0, cenário b).
@servicoSeedId = a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
@insumoSeedId = b2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002
@insumoSemEstoqueId = b2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003

# Cole aqui o token do e-mail simulado (passo 6).
@tokenOrcamento = cole-o-token-do-log-do-billing

###############################################################################
# 1. Logins
###############################################################################

# @name loginAdmin
POST {{os}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@oficina.local", "senha": "admin123" }

###

# @name loginAtendente
POST {{os}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "atendente@oficina.local", "senha": "senha123" }

###

# @name loginMecanico
POST {{os}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "mecanico@oficina.local", "senha": "senha123" }

###

@admin = {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}
@atendente = {{loginAtendente.response.body.accessToken}}
@mecanico = {{loginMecanico.response.body.accessToken}}

###############################################################################
# 2. Catalog: serviço e insumo novos (ou use os ids do seed acima)
# O código do insumo é único: numa segunda execução troque "OLEO-VIDEO" (senão 409 INSUMO_CODIGO_DUPLICADO).
###############################################################################

# @name servico
POST {{catalog}}/servicos
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "nome": "Troca de óleo (vídeo)", "descricao": "Troca de óleo e filtro", "valorPadrao": 150 }

###

# @name insumo
POST {{catalog}}/insumos
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "codigo": "OLEO-VIDEO", "nome": "Óleo 5W30", "tipo": "INSUMO", "valorUnitario": 45.5, "quantidadeEstoque": 100 }

###

@servicoId = {{servico.response.body.id}}
@insumoId = {{insumo.response.body.id}}

###############################################################################
# 3. Abrir a OS (atendente). Status RECEBIDA; a saga pede o diagnóstico ao Execution.
###############################################################################

# @name abrir
POST {{os}}/ordens-de-servico
Authorization: Bearer {{atendente}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "clienteId": "{{clienteId}}", "veiculoId": "{{veiculoId}}", "observacoes": "Barulho no motor" }

###

@osId = {{abrir.response.body.id}}
@numeroOs = {{abrir.response.body.numero}}

###############################################################################
# 4. Diagnóstico (mecânico)
###############################################################################

# A OS chega ao Execution de forma assíncrona: 404 até o enfileirar-diagnostico ser consumido.
# Resposta: { ordem: { status: AGUARDANDO_DIAGNOSTICO, itens, ... }, historico }.
GET {{execution}}/ordens/{{osId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{mecanico}}

###

POST {{execution}}/{{osId}}/diagnostico/iniciar
Authorization: Bearer {{mecanico}}

###

# Itens só entram com a OS em EM_DIAGNOSTICO (preço vem do Catalog).
POST {{os}}/ordens-de-servico/{{osId}}/itens
Authorization: Bearer {{mecanico}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tipo": "SERVICO", "referenciaId": "{{servicoId}}", "quantidade": 1 }

###

POST {{os}}/ordens-de-servico/{{osId}}/itens
Authorization: Bearer {{mecanico}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tipo": "INSUMO", "referenciaId": "{{insumoId}}", "quantidade": 2 }

###

# Conclui o diagnóstico: o OS pede o orçamento ao Billing, que manda o e-mail (simulado).
POST {{execution}}/{{osId}}/diagnostico/concluir
Authorization: Bearer {{mecanico}}

###############################################################################
# 5. OS em AGUARDANDO_APROVACAO, com valorTotal e etapaSaga ORCAMENTO (assíncrono: repita se ainda EM_DIAGNOSTICO)
###############################################################################

GET {{os}}/ordens-de-servico/{{osId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

###

GET {{os}}/ordens-de-servico/{{osId}}/historico
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

###############################################################################
# 6. Token do orçamento
# O e-mail é um log do Billing ("E-mail enviado (simulado)") com o link
# .../publico/orcamentos/<numero>?token=<token>. No terminal:
#   docker compose -f local/docker-compose.yml logs billing | grep token=
# Copie o token da OS certa e cole em @tokenOrcamento lá em cima.
###############################################################################

###############################################################################
# 7. Cliente vê o orçamento e aprova (rotas públicas, sem JWT)
###############################################################################

GET {{billing}}/publico/orcamentos/{{numeroOs}}?token={{tokenOrcamento}}

###

# Aprovar → reserva de insumos → pivô (execucao-aceita).
# Depois do aceite a OS continua APROVADA, com etapaSaga EXECUCAO; no Execution a ordem fica
# AGUARDANDO_REPARO. A OS só vira EM_EXECUCAO com o reparo-iniciado (passo 8).
POST {{billing}}/publico/orcamentos/{{numeroOs}}/decisao
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "{{tokenOrcamento}}", "decisao": "APROVADA" }

###

GET {{os}}/ordens-de-servico/{{osId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

###############################################################################
# 8. Reparo (mecânico)
###############################################################################

# @name reparoIniciar
POST {{execution}}/{{osId}}/reparo/iniciar
Authorization: Bearer {{mecanico}}

###

@itemId = {{reparoIniciar.response.body.$.itens[0].itemId}}

POST {{execution}}/{{osId}}/itens/{{itemId}}/apontamento
Authorization: Bearer {{mecanico}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "acao": "INICIAR" }

###

POST {{execution}}/{{osId}}/itens/{{itemId}}/apontamento
Authorization: Bearer {{mecanico}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "acao": "FINALIZAR" }

###

# Libera a vaga; o OS vai a FINALIZADA e pede baixa do estoque + cobrança.
POST {{execution}}/{{osId}}/reparo/concluir
Authorization: Bearer {{mecanico}}

###############################################################################
# 9. Cobrança, pagamento e entrega
###############################################################################

# A cobrança é assíncrona (gerar-cobranca): repita até aparecer uma PENDENTE.
# Com PAYMENT_PROVIDER=fake o initPoint aponta para o próprio /dev/pagamentos/<osId>/simular.
GET {{billing}}/cobrancas/{{osId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

###

# 404 enquanto não houver cobrança PENDENTE.
POST {{billing}}/dev/pagamentos/{{osId}}/simular
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "aprovado": true }

###

# Com a OS PAGA:
POST {{os}}/ordens-de-servico/{{osId}}/entrega
Authorization: Bearer {{atendente}}

###

GET {{os}}/ordens-de-servico/{{osId}}/historico
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

###

# Estoque baixado: quantidadeEstoque 98, quantidadeReservada 0.
GET {{catalog}}/insumos/{{insumoId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

###############################################################################
# 10. Status público da OS (referência)
# Exige token de CLIENTE emitido pela Lambda de autenticação por CPF (Etapa 7);
# com o token de funcionário responde 403.
###############################################################################

GET {{os}}/publico/os/{{numeroOs}}/status
Authorization: Bearer <token-de-cliente-da-lambda>

###############################################################################
# 11. Cenários de falha (abra uma OS nova e repita os passos 3 a 7 com a diferença indicada)
###############################################################################

# (a) Reprovação: no passo 7 mande "REPROVADA". A OS termina REPROVADA (saga ENCERRADA).
POST {{billing}}/publico/orcamentos/{{numeroOs}}/decisao
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "{{tokenOrcamento}}", "decisao": "REPROVADA" }

###

# (b) Sem estoque: no passo 4 use o insumo PAS-001 do seed (estoque 0) e aprove no passo 7.
# A reserva falha, o Billing cancela o orçamento ("Não há estoque suficiente...") e a OS vira CANCELADA.
POST {{os}}/ordens-de-servico/{{osId}}/itens
Authorization: Bearer {{mecanico}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tipo": "INSUMO", "referenciaId": "{{insumoSemEstoqueId}}", "quantidade": 2 }

###

# (c) Fila cheia: o compose usa EXECUTION_MAX_CONCURRENT=1. Com uma OS aceita ainda sem
# reparo/concluir, aprove uma segunda OS: o Execution recusa (CAPACIDADE_ESGOTADA), o Catalog
# libera as reservas, o Billing cancela ("A oficina está sem capacidade...") e a segunda OS vira CANCELADA.
GET {{execution}}/fila
Authorization: Bearer {{mecanico}}

###

# (d) Pagamento recusado: no passo 9 simule com aprovado=false. A OS continua FINALIZADA, o histórico
# ganha "Pagamento recusado" e o Billing gera nova cobrança PENDENTE (a anterior fica RECUSADA).
# Com o fake o initPoint da nova cobrança é igual ao da anterior: compare pelo id em /cobrancas.
POST {{billing}}/dev/pagamentos/{{osId}}/simular
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "aprovado": false }

###

GET {{billing}}/cobrancas/{{osId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
